# Efficiency allowlist — read by crates/marion-testsupport/tests/three_axis (run: scripts/three-axis.sh).
#
# Format: `path:item  one-line reason`. A finding not listed here fails the check; an entry nothing
# matches fails it too, so a fix deletes its line. THIS LIST ONLY SHRINKS. The perf waves are
# replacing these timer-driven waits with event-driven ones (poll(2)/kqueue, condvars, pipes);
# a bounded one-shot wait with a clear deadline may stay, and says so.

# --- tracked: efficiency waves ------------------------------------------------------------------
crates/marion-supervisor/src/serve.rs:ACCEPT_POLL  poll(2) timeout floor only: the accept loop blocks in poll(2) on the listeners and wakes on a connection or a handle deadline; 5 ms bounds a readable-but-vanished listener (perf-wave1 2da8ea8)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/serve.rs:run_conn_writer  blocks in recv(); the try_recv loop only drains what is queued after the connection departed, then ends (perf-wave1 74d9b38)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/detach.rs:REGISTRY_POLL  backstop only: the follower wakes on the journal write notification (kqueue/inotify, wake.rs); a 1 s re-read catches a missed event (perf-wave1 05e8272)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/detach.rs:ENTITLEMENT_POLL  backstop only: the supervisor lock is watched for changes; a 5 s re-check bounds a missed event (perf-wave1 b5e6fa7)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/detach.rs:watch_entitlement  waits on the lock files' change watches; sleeps ENTITLEMENT_POLL only on a platform with no watch (perf-wave1 b5e6fa7)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/detach.rs:DIAL_POLL  tracked: efficiency waves (5 ms dial retry period)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/detach.rs:ensure_supervisor_within  tracked: efficiency waves (dial-retry sleep loop until a deadline)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/registry.rs:LiveRegistry::follow  waits on the journal write pipe and file watch; sleeps its interval only where neither exists (perf-wave1 05e8272)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/pty.rs:POLL  tracked: efficiency waves (5 ms pty poll)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/pty.rs:PtyMaster::write_all  tracked: efficiency waves (sleep-and-retry on a full pty)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/root.rs:PANE_POLL  tracked: efficiency waves (25 ms pane-exit poll)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/root.rs:wait_for_the_pane_to_end  tracked: efficiency waves (sleep(PANE_POLL) loop)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/run.rs:DRAIN_POLL_MS  tracked: efficiency waves (20 ms drain poll)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/run.rs:Drain::finish  tracked: efficiency waves (DRAIN_POLL_MS sleep loop)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/run.rs:run_bounded_with  tracked: efficiency waves (try_wait + sleep loop on the child)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/duplex.rs:watchdog  tracked: efficiency waves (duplex watchdog sleep loop)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/duplex.rs:run_duplex  tracked: efficiency waves (recv_timeout on a fixed period)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/descendant_gate.rs:HOLD_POLL  partial: a held node re-reads its subtree only when the registry changed (perf-wave1 95ec1bf); the 100 ms pause remains where no follower reads the journal
crates/marion-supervisor/src/rpc.rs:Driver::settle_until  bounded: waits on the reader/inbox condvar; try_wait is the one non-event check, once per LIVENESS_TICK (2 s) while a node is live, for a server that died with its stdout still held
crates/marion-supervisor/src/rpc.rs:LIVENESS_TICK  bounded: the safety bound on a condvar wait (2 s), never the ordinary path — see Driver::settle_until
crates/marion-supervisor/src/acp_child.rs:prompt_session  bounded: the held-inbox wait blocks on the shared driver's condvar (rpc::Driver::wait_event); try_wait once per wake or LIVENESS_TICK (2 s)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/native_relay.rs:POLL  tracked: efficiency waves (50 ms native relay tick)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/native_relay.rs:RawPaneSession::start_keyboard  tracked: efficiency waves (keyboard thread sleep loop)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/native_relay.rs:RawPaneSession::open_with_io  tracked: efficiency waves (read timeout as the relay tick)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/attach.rs:POLL  tracked: efficiency waves (50 ms attach poll)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/attach.rs:run  tracked: efficiency waves (read timeout as the attach tick)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/attach.rs:Session::open_with_terminal  tracked: efficiency waves (read timeout as the attach tick)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/tree.rs:POLL  tracked: efficiency waves (50 ms tree poll)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/tree.rs:dial  tracked: efficiency waves (read timeout as the tree tick)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/bin/marion.rs:JOURNAL_POLL  backstop only: marion run tails the journal on write notifications; a 1 s re-read bounds a missed event (perf-wave1 bba68e0)

# --- untracked: first found by the three-axis check; reported, not yet scheduled ----------------
crates/marion-supervisor/src/continuation.rs:OWED_POLL  untracked: 100 ms owed-turn poll period
crates/marion-supervisor/src/handler.rs:Broadcast::start  untracked: broadcast thread sleeps in a loop
crates/marion-supervisor/src/doctor.rs:AcpChild::response  untracked: doctor's ACP probe sleeps in a loop for a response (one-shot command, bounded)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/socket.rs:acquire_within  untracked: sleep loop acquiring the socket lock until a deadline

# --- bounded one-shot waits with a clear deadline -----------------------------------------------
crates/marion-supervisor/src/native_bootstrap.rs:exchange_native_claim  bounded: one claim exchange under LAUNCH_RESULT_TIMEOUT, then reset to blocking
crates/marion-supervisor/src/bin/marion.rs:SupervisorSession::request_detach_all  bounded: one request/response under SUPERVISOR_REPLY_WAIT
crates/marion-supervisor/src/handler.rs:ATTACHED_TICK  tracked: efficiency waves — 5 ms re-read of a followed node's events.jsonl, only while a client is attached to it (the accept loop itself now blocks in poll(2)); remove when a per-node file watch wakes it
crates/marion-supervisor/src/wake.rs:poll_until  bounded one-shot wait: the one sleep-until-deadline loop, for a child's exit or a file nothing can wake on; every caller passes its own budget (ready file, INTERRUPT_GRACE, SUPERVISOR_EXIT_WAIT)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/kill.rs:observe_dead  bounded one-shot wait: reads a killed process's state with backoff (1 ms doubling to OBSERVE_PAUSE_MAX) until it is gone or the kill deadline passes, so the kill confirmation is earned; never runs idle

# --- home-polish (2026-09-27): the event-driven home loop ---------------------------------------
crates/marion-supervisor/src/home/session.rs:TICK  bounded: the home screen wakes on it only while something on the tab moves (a running node's elapsed time, a harness being checked); an idle screen has no timeout at all
crates/marion-supervisor/src/home/session.rs:Session::reports  not a poll: drains the side threads' channel once the wake pipe says a report arrived; never loops on a timer
